# Wave W17-AC (Route 227): stark turf — hot grass under ash, grey creep at the edges: a hot olive grass carrying grey ash-creep flecks where the fall from Grim Mountain drifts over it, cooling toward the ash field it surrounds (design: ash on the wind, heat in the stone). The shipped ashground biome stands byte-identical entire at the field’s heart (Ruling #3) — this turf is the grass the ash falls ON. Route 227’s own ground — split from its twin Route 225’s scorched turf by register entire (grey creep on hot grass vs rust-ochre hardpan) and from Maris’s swept turf by heat: Borea’s ash falls on hot volcanic grass, Maris’s on cool swept fields.
